@page "/"
@using System.Runtime.InteropServices
@inject IBonboardingService BonboardingService

<PageTitle>Bonboarding samples</PageTitle>

<h1>Bonboarding samples</h1>

<p>
    The same tours, hints and checklist, hosted unchanged in every Blazor hosting model: Server, WebAssembly, Auto and
    MAUI (Blazor Hybrid). Whichever runs these pages, every decision about a tour is made in C#, and the library's one
    small module measures, observes and routes keys in the page.
</p>

<h2>This host</h2>
<dl class="facts">
    <dt>Renderer</dt>
    <dd>@RendererInfo.Name (@(RendererInfo.IsInteractive ? "interactive" : "prerendering - interactive in a moment"))</dd>
    <dt>.NET runs on</dt>
    <dd>@(OperatingSystem.IsBrowser() ? "the browser (WebAssembly)" : RuntimeInformation.OSDescription)</dd>
    <dt>Progress is stored in</dt>
    <dd>the page's <code>localStorage</code>, through JS interop</dd>
</dl>

<p class="muted">
    The welcome tour started by itself the first time this app was opened, and not again once it was finished or
    closed. Reset everything on the <a href="progress">progress page</a> to see it start again.
</p>

<div class="row">
    <button type="button" @onclick="StartWelcomeAsync" disabled="@(RendererInfo.IsInteractive is false)">Take the welcome tour</button>
</div>

<h2>Pages</h2>
<ul>
    <li><a href="workspace">Workspace</a> - a tour across two routes, with a step that waits for the page to raise a signal</li>
    <li><a href="guidance">Guidance</a> - a beacon with a hint, a checklist and a list of tours</li>
    <li><a href="progress">Progress</a> - the stored records and the live event stream</li>
</ul>

@code {
    // Resumes where the user left it, or starts from the top once it was finished.
    private Task StartWelcomeAsync() => BonboardingService.StartAsync(SampleTours.WelcomeId);
}
